  "cleanText": "Solution home \n\t\tBookkeeping\n\t\tBookkeeping FAQs\n\n### How to enter a supplier refund that was paid into the bank account?\n\n\t\t\tPrint\n\n\tModified on: Thu, 25 Nov, 2021 at 12:53 PM\n\nNavigation:  Bookkeeping > Sales/Purchases > Invoices\n\nHelp/Guide:\n\nYou may raise the Credit note under the purchases section. \n\nNavigate to the Sales/Purchase Invoice page from the navigation above, click on New Invoice then change the invoice type to Credit Note from the drop down (see below)\n\nThen please head to the bank account \n\nNavigation:  Bookkeeping > Bank > Dashboard > Select Bank\n\nPlease select refund from the action dropdown next to the transactions\n\nThe following pop up will appear, please enter the details of the credit note and the amount to allocate.\n\nThen click save.\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tDid you find it helpful?\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tYes\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tNo\n\nSend feedback\tSorry we couldn't be helpful. Help us improve this article with your feedback.",
